# Typography: Hyphenate with the patterns of the language, the soft hyphen, and the hyphens written inside a word.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · Hyphenation
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 30
			Vertical: top
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
		For style: column
			Box:
				Width: 120
				Padding: 0 0 0 8
				Border: 0 0 0 0.5
				Border color: rule
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Align: justify
				Language: en-GB
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Hyphenation
		Paragraph: With `Hyphenate: true`, words are split at the end of a line with the patterns of the `Language` of the box (es, ca, en-US, en-GB, de, fr, it, nl and pt). A soft hyphen (U+00AD) marks a break point by hand, and a hyphen between letters or digits is always one.
			Style: intro
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Hyphenate: false
						Style: label
					Paragraph: Internationalisation of the administrative documentation requires considerable organisational commitment.
						Style: column
						Typography:
							Hyphenate: false
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Hyphenate: true
						Style: label
					Paragraph: Internationalisation of the administrative documentation requires considerable organisational commitment.
						Style: column
						Typography:
							Hyphenate: true
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Language: de, Hyphenate: true
						Style: label
					Paragraph: Die Donaudampfschifffahrtsgesellschaft veröffentlicht ihre Jahresabschlussberichte.
						Style: column
						Typography:
							Language: de
							Hyphenate: true
		Text: A soft hyphen inside a word, without Hyphenate  (Ther|mo|stat|con|trol|ler)
			Style: label
		Paragraph: The new Ther­mo­stat­con­trol­ler unit replaces the old one.
			Style: column
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
		Text: A written hyphen is a break point, a non-breaking hyphen (U+2011) is not
			Style: label
